### =========================================================================
### GO REST API STARTER KIT - HTTP REQUEST COLLECTION (REST CLIENT)
### Auth (JWT + RTR), User Management, Granular RBAC, Admin Users, & Content Modules
### =========================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

# Insert the access token obtained from login / register / refresh response:
@accessToken = 
@refreshToken = 

# Insert verification / reset token obtained from LogMailer console or Resend inbox:
@sampleToken = 

# Replace with actual ULID when testing detail / update / delete endpoints:
@sampleArticleId = 01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5FAV
@sampleCategoryId = 01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5FC1
@sampleTagId = 01M7TAG0000000000000000001
@sampleMediaId = 01M7MED0000000000000000001
@sampleRoleId = 01M7ECAYAE7NB3X6BT4BK3DKAQ
@samplePermissionId = 01M7ECAYAE7NB3X6BT4BK3DKB1
@sampleUserId = 01M7ECBRK61JN9T5ANTCF1THVP


### =========================================================================
### 0. SYSTEM HEALTH & READINESS PROBES
### =========================================================================

### 0.1 Full System Health Check (Checks Database Connection & Pool)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 0.2 Liveness Probe (Instant Container Lifecycle Verification)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### 0.3 Readiness Probe (Traffic Routing Ingress Check)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready


### =========================================================================
### 1. AUTHENTICATION (JWT + REFRESH TOKEN ROTATION)
### =========================================================================

### 1.1 Register New Account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "johndoe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "full_name": "John Doe"
}

### 1.2 Login Account (Admin / User)
# Generates JWT access_token and refresh_token, and sets HTTP-only cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@mmdbconnect.com",
  "password": "adminpassword123"
}

### 1.3 Refresh Token (via JSON Body)
# Can be sent via JSON body, automatic HTTP-only cookie, or X-Refresh-Token header
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 1.3b Refresh Token (via X-Refresh-Token Header)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
X-Refresh-Token: {{refreshToken}}

### 1.4 Logout (Revoke Session & Clear Cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 1.5 Change Account Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "old_password": "adminpassword123",
  "new_password": "newadminpassword123"
}

### 1.6 Forgot Password Request
# Anti-enumeration: always returns 200 OK. Token printed to console (LogMailer) or sent via Resend
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@mmdbconnect.com"
}

### 1.7 Reset Password (Using Token)
# Token obtained from console/email (can be set to @sampleToken variable above).
# All existing refresh token sessions will be automatically revoked upon successful reset.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{sampleToken}}",
  "new_password": "newpassword12345"
}

### 1.8 Verify Email (Token via Query Parameter)
# Accepts token via query parameter or JSON body (POST to avoid crawler/scanner consumption)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-email?token={{sampleToken}}

### 1.9 Verify Email (Token via JSON Body)
# Alternative for mobile app or API clients
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{sampleToken}}"
}

### 1.10 Resend Verification Email
# Anti-enumeration: always returns 200 OK. Old pending tokens are revoked automatically.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@mmdbconnect.com"
}


### =========================================================================
### 2. USER MANAGEMENT (/api/v1/users)
### =========================================================================

### 2.1 Get Current User Profile (/me)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.2 Update Profile Information
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Mochammad Bagas Pratama",
  "bio": "Software Engineer & Backend Enthusiast",
  "phone_number": "081234567890"
}

### 2.3 Update Username
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/username
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bagaspratama"
}

### 2.4 Check Account Status & Email Verification
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/status
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.5 Upload Profile Avatar (Multipart Form Data)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="avatar"; filename="avatar.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./testdata/sample.png
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

### 2.6 Delete Avatar
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.7 Request Email Change
# Requires authentication & current password confirmation. Verification token sent to new email.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/email/request-change
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "new_email": "bagas.new@example.com",
  "password": "adminpassword123"
}

### 2.8 Confirm Email Change (Token via Query Parameter)
# Accepts token via query parameter or JSON body (POST to avoid crawler/scanner consumption)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/email/confirm-change?token={{sampleToken}}

### 2.9 Confirm Email Change (Token via JSON Body)
# Alternative for mobile / API clients
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/email/confirm-change
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{sampleToken}}"
}


### =========================================================================
### 3. PUBLIC ARTICLES & TAXONOMY (Read-Only & Event Ingestion)
### =========================================================================

### 3.1 List Published Articles (Pagination, Filters & Search)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/articles?page=1&per_page=10&search=&category=&tag=&is_featured=

### 3.2 Article Detail by Slug
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/articles/building-rest-apis-with-go

### 3.3 Record Article Analytics Event (Idempotent via X-Event-ID or JSON)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/articles/{{sampleArticleId}}/analytics
Content-Type: application/json
X-Event-ID: evt_01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5FA1
X-Session-ID: sess_987654321

{
  "event_id": "evt_01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5FA1",
  "session_id": "sess_987654321",
  "event_type": "view",
  "reading_time_seconds": 45,
  "scroll_depth": 75
}

### 3.4 List All Public Categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories

### 3.5 Articles by Category Slug
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/tutorials-tech/articles?page=1&per_page=10

### 3.6 List All Public Tags
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tags

### 3.7 Public Tag Detail by Slug
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tags/golang

### 3.8 SEO-Friendly URL Alias
GET {{baseUrl}}/articles/building-rest-apis-with-go


### =========================================================================
### 4. ADMIN: ARTICLE, TAXONOMY, MEDIA & ANALYTICS MANAGEMENT
### =========================================================================

### 4.1 List All Articles (Draft, Scheduled, Published, Archived)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles?page=1&per_page=10&status=&category_id=&author_id=&search=
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.2 Create New Article (XSS Cleaned HTML & Automatic ULID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Optimizing MySQL and Go REST Architecture",
  "slug": "optimizing-mysql-and-go-rest-architecture",
  "excerpt": "Comprehensive architectural guide covering ULID, connection pools, and SQLC.",
  "content": "<h2>Architecture Deep Dive</h2><p>Here is an embedded diagram:</p><p><img src=\"http://localhost:8080/uploads/diag.png\" data-media-id=\"{{sampleMediaId}}\" alt=\"Architecture Diagram\" /></p>",
  "category_id": "{{sampleCategoryId}}",
  "featured_image_id": "{{sampleMediaId}}",
  "og_image_id": "{{sampleMediaId}}",
  "tags": ["Go", "MySQL", "Clean Architecture"],
  "related_ids": [],
  "meta_title": "Optimizing MySQL and Go REST Architecture",
  "meta_description": "Best practices for high-concurrency Go REST backends.",
  "is_featured": true,
  "robots_index": true,
  "robots_follow": true,
  "status": "published"
}

### 4.3 Article Detail by ULID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles/{{sampleArticleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.4 Update Article by ULID (Creates Revision Snapshot Automatically)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles/{{sampleArticleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Optimizing MySQL and Go REST Architecture (Revised Edition)",
  "slug": "optimizing-mysql-and-go-rest-architecture",
  "excerpt": "Comprehensive architectural guide covering ULID, connection pools, and SQLC.",
  "content": "<h2>Architecture Deep Dive v2</h2><p>Revised content with updated benchmarks.</p>",
  "category_id": "{{sampleCategoryId}}",
  "featured_image_id": "{{sampleMediaId}}",
  "tags": ["Go", "MySQL", "Performance"],
  "is_featured": true,
  "status": "published"
}

### 4.5 Delete Article by ULID (Soft Delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles/{{sampleArticleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.6 List Article Historical Revisions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles/{{sampleArticleId}}/revisions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.7 List All Categories (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.7b Get Category by ULID (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{sampleCategoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.8 Create New Category
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cloud & DevOps",
  "slug": "cloud-devops",
  "description": "Cloud computing, infrastructure as code, and container orchestration."
}

### 4.9 Update Category by ULID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{sampleCategoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cloud Architecture & DevOps",
  "slug": "cloud-architecture-devops",
  "description": "Enterprise cloud architecture and DevOps practices."
}

### 4.10 Delete Category by ULID (Protected if Category Has Articles)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{sampleCategoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.11 List All Tags (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.12 Create New Tag
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Microservices",
  "slug": "microservices"
}

### 4.13 Update Tag by ULID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tags/{{sampleTagId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Distributed Systems",
  "slug": "distributed-systems"
}

### 4.14 Delete Tag by ULID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/tags/{{sampleTagId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.15 Upload Media Asset (Image Sniffing, Renaming & Metadata Extraction)
# Supports form field 'image' or 'file' (max 10MB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/media
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="cover-banner.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./test_uploads/sample.png
--WebAppBoundary--

### 4.16 List Media Library (Paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/media?page=1&per_page=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.17 Media Detail by ULID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/media/{{sampleMediaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.18 Delete Media by ULID (Protected if Media is In Use)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/media/{{sampleMediaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.19 Get Article Daily Analytics Report (Aggregated by Worker)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/articles/{{sampleArticleId}}/analytics?start_date=2026-01-01&end_date=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.20 Get Global System Analytics Overview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/analytics/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### =========================================================================
### 5. RBAC MANAGEMENT (ROLES & PERMISSIONS)
### =========================================================================

@sampleRoleId = 01M7ECAYAE7NB3X6BT4BK3DKAQ
@samplePermissionId = 01M7ECAYAE7NB3X6BT4BK3DKB1

### 5.1 List All Roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.2 Role Detail by ULID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/roles/{{sampleRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.3 Create New Role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "editor",
  "display_name": "Content Editor",
  "description": "Can manage posts and view user listings"
}

### 5.4 Update Role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/roles/{{sampleRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "display_name": "Senior Content Editor",
  "description": "Senior level editor access"
}

### 5.5 Assign Permissions to Role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/roles/{{sampleRoleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "permission_ids": [
    "{{samplePermissionId}}"
  ]
}

### 5.6 Delete Role
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/roles/{{sampleRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.7 List All Permissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.8 Permission Detail by ULID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/permissions/{{samplePermissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.9 Create New Permission
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "reports.export",
  "description": "Download and export system reports"
}

### 5.10 Update Permission Description
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/permissions/{{samplePermissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Download spreadsheet and PDF report files"
}

### 5.11 Delete Permission
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/permissions/{{samplePermissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### =========================================================================
### 6. ADMIN USER MANAGEMENT
### =========================================================================

@sampleUserId = 01M7ECBRK61JN9T5ANTCF1THVP

### 6.1 List All Users (Search, Filter, Pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users?page=1&limit=10&search=&status=active&role=
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6.2 Get Complete User Details (Profile & Roles)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{sampleUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6.3 Update User Information by Admin
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{sampleUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bagas_updated",
  "email": "bagas.new@example.com",
  "full_name": "Mochammad Bagas Triadi",
  "bio": "Software Engineer & Backend Enthusiast",
  "phone_number": "+6281234567890"
}

### 6.4 Update User Account Status (active / inactive / pending_verification / suspended)
# Note: Protected against deactivating or suspending the last active Super Admin (HTTP 403)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{sampleUserId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "suspended"
}

### 6.5 Assign Roles to User
# Note: Protected against revoking Super Admin role from the last active Super Admin (HTTP 403)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{sampleUserId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_ids": [
    "{{sampleRoleId}}"
  ]
}

### 6.6 Delete User Account
# Note: Protected against deleting the last active Super Admin (HTTP 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{sampleUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
